secure-terminal-review(1) -- show the review popup by itself
============================================================

<!--
# Copyright (C) 2026 - 2026 ENCRYPTED SUPPORT LLC <adrelanos@whonix.org>
# See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
-->

## SYNOPSIS

`secure-terminal-review` [`--kind` paste|copy|clipboard] [`--text` TEXT]
[`--theme` THEME] [`--delay` SECONDS]

## DESCRIPTION

secure-terminal-review shows the secure-terminal review popup on its own, with
no terminal, tab or pseudo-terminal behind it. It hosts the SAME review widget
the docked review bar (in the terminal window) and the clipboard sanitizer use,
so the transforms, the fully-revealed per-character view, the content-driven
Deliver gate and the direction wording are all identical -- this is only a
separate frame for that one widget.

The payload to review is `--text` if given, otherwise text piped on standard
input, otherwise a small built-in sample that contains hidden characters so the
bar has something to reveal. The user's choice is printed to standard output and
the process exits: `rejected` for Reject, or the exact delivered text (the box
contents plus the neutralized tail) for Deliver.

It needs a running graphical session (a Wayland or X display), like the terminal
itself.

## OPTIONS

  * `--kind` paste|copy|clipboard:
    The review direction, which sets the button wording and the accept note.
    Default: paste.

  * `--text` TEXT:
    The text to review. Overrides standard input and the built-in sample.

  * `--theme` THEME:
    The colour theme of the preview panes. Default: the configured theme.

  * `--delay` SECONDS:
    The anti-fat-finger countdown that gates Deliver, in seconds. Default: 0.

## EXIT STATUS

Exits with the Qt application's exit code (0 on a normal close).

## SEE ALSO

`secure-terminal`(1)
